#, kde-kuit-format
msgctxt "@info:usagetip"
msgid ""
"Tell us what works on your screens and what does not. Copy what your screens "
"can do in 3D, then report it with what you saw."
msgstr ""

#, kde-kuit-format
msgctxt "@info:usagetip"
msgid ""
"The window under the pointer is the one that gets your keys. Move the "
"pointer onto a window and type: there is nothing to click. Leave the pointer "
"there for a moment and the window comes to the front.<nl/><nl/>Why: fewer "
"clicks and faster workflows, and fewer health problems as a result. Your "
"mouse lasts longer too.<nl/><nl/>If what you type does not appear, look "
"where the pointer is. To work another way, open Window Behavior in System "
"Settings and choose how a window gets the focus."
msgstr ""

